Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cpu-arm.c
Line: 347
Function: arm_check_note
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: The bounds check uses namesz + descsz + offsetof(arm_Note, name) on unsigned long, which can wrap on 32-bit hosts when descsz is large, allowing the check to pass erroneously. Callers may then trust pointers into buffer beyond its end, enabling out-of-bounds reads/writes (e.g., subsequent strcmp/strcpy in bfd_arm_update_notes).

